---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ORGANIZATION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
    title={`About ${ORGANIZATION.name} | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
    description={`The student-run AI team at ${ORGANIZATION.fullUniversity}.`}
>
    <article class="team-page-container reveal-on-scroll">
        <header class="page-header">
            <h1>About {ORGANIZATION.name}</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">The student-run AI team at {ORGANIZATION.fullUniversity}</p>
            <hr />
        </header>

        <div class="team-hero-image">
            <img src="/us.jpg" alt={`The ${ORGANIZATION.name} team`} />
        </div>

        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                <strong>"{ORGANIZATION.name}"</strong> means <em>Let us calculate</em>. It's a phrase from Leibniz, who wanted to solve problems purely through computation. We're a team of computer science and AI students of <strong>{ORGANIZATION.fullUniversity}</strong> solving challenges of the current (scientific) community.
            </p>

            <h3>What we do</h3>
            <p>
                We focus on the mechanics of artificial intelligence, by participating all kinds of AI-related challenges. We like to puzzle and be creative. Our team consists of AI engineers, coordinators and team managers.
            </p>

            <h3>The Community</h3>
            <p>
                Studying AI is easier (and a lot more fun) when you aren't doing it alone. {ORGANIZATION.name} acts as a place for students who want to build, debug, or research together. We run a few main events throughout the year:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Tech Talks:</strong> Technical deep dives by ({ORGANIZATION.department}) researchers and industry.</li>
                <li><strong>Hackathons:</strong> Short (and highly energized) sprints to build working models from scratch.</li>
                <li><strong>Game Nights:</strong> Low-key evenings where we bring laptops, grab pizza, and try to beat our self-made agents.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>On top of that, we host interviews with current leaders and pioneers in the AI landscape. Feel free to reach out if you're having an interesting research-topic.</p>

            <h3>Join us</h3>
            <p>
                Whether you're a master's student training models for your thesis or a first-year who just wrote their first PyTorch training loop, you're welcome here. Check out our <a href="/events">Events</a> page to see when we're meeting next.
            </p>
        </div>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .team-page-container {
        max-width: var(--max-width-main);
        margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .page-header {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .page-header h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        color: var(--black);
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    .subtitle {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: var(--gray-slate);
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .team-hero-image {
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }
    .team-hero-image img {
        width: 100%;
        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
        box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        display: block;
    }
    .prose {
        color: var(--gray-slate);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }
    .prose h3 {
        color: var(--black);
        margin-top: 2em;
        margin-bottom: 0.75em;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
    .prose p, .prose li {
        color: var(--gray-slate);
        margin-bottom: 1.5em;
    }
    .prose strong {
        color: var(--black);
    }
</style>